    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0207" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg119"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/57</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1483</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-03">April 3, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged of your
                    despatch No. 1401, dated March 8, 1933, in which you set forth your views and
                    report the representations <pb facs="0208" n="120" xml:id="pg120"/> made by the
                    Embassy with a view to obtaining equivalent treatment for American interests to
                    that granted to other foreign nations by Chile’s various compensation
                    agreements.</p>
                <p>The Department appreciates the Embassy’s constructive interest in this matter and
                    hereby approves the views which you have conveyed to the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs in your notes of February 23 and March 3, 1933.<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d111-f1"/></p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis
                            White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
